 <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">

 <!-- Answer-first TL;DR -->
 <aside class="mb-10 border border-hairline bg-panel p-7">
 <p class="mb-3 font-mono text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-gold-700">Quick Answer</p>
 <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal sm:text-xl speakable-answer">A company shirt is a branded shirt that identifies a business — typically a polo, tee, work shirt, or hoodie with the company logo applied via embroidery or screen printing. They're worn by employees so customers, suppliers, and the public can identify the business at a glance.</p>
 </aside>

 <h2 id="names" class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-charcoal">What Are Company Shirts Called?</h2>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">The category goes by several names depending on industry: <strong>branded apparel</strong>, <strong>corporate apparel</strong>, <strong>custom workwear</strong>, <strong>uniform shirts</strong>, <strong>logo wear</strong>, or just <strong>company uniforms</strong>. In trades and construction, "crew shirts" and "service shirts" are common. Promotional industry distributors usually call the broader category "<a href="https://www.promoproducts.com/" rel="noopener" class="text-gold-700 underline decoration-gold-500/40 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-gold-600">promotional products</a>" or "decorated apparel."</p>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">It's worth knowing that "company shirt" is broader than just t-shirts. The category includes polos, button-down work shirts, hoodies, jackets, hi-vis safety apparel, hats, and even branded coveralls.</p>

 <h2 id="types" class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-charcoal">The Main Types of Company Shirts</h2>

 <h3 class="mt-8 mb-3 font-heading text-xl font-bold">Polos</h3>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">The default for service techs, customer-facing staff, and management. Embroidered chest logo, often with the employee's name. Looks professional at a customer's house, on a sales call, or at a trade show. Port Authority K500 is the workhorse SKU.</p>

 <h3 class="mt-8 mb-3 font-heading text-xl font-bold">T-Shirts</h3>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">The everyday shirt for field crews. Heavyweight cotton or moisture-wicking poly blends, screen-printed back logo, smaller chest logo. Carhartt K87 and Bayside 5100 are the heavyweight standards. See our guide on <a href="/screen-printing-vs-embroidery-construction-las-vegas/" class="text-gold-700 underline decoration-gold-500/40 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-gold-600">screen printing vs. embroidery</a> for which decoration to pick.</p>

 <h3 class="mt-8 mb-3 font-heading text-xl font-bold">Work Shirts</h3>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">Mechanic-style button-down shirts may suit HVAC, plumbing, mechanical, and customer-facing service roles. Compare the exact garment, decoration, laundry-provider requirements, care, and expected use rather than assuming a universal lifespan advantage.</p>

 <h3 class="mt-8 mb-3 font-heading text-xl font-bold">Hoodies + Jackets</h3>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">For cool desert mornings, pre-dawn starts, and winter work. Heavyweight cotton-blend hoodies for general use; insulated jackets for the cold months. Embroidered chest logo, sometimes with a screen-printed back.</p>

 <h3 class="mt-8 mb-3 font-heading text-xl font-bold">Hi-Vis Safety Apparel</h3>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">The employer and safety lead determine whether high-visibility apparel is required for a task or site. Any decoration must follow the exact garment manufacturer's current written instructions and the employer's policy.</p>

 <h2 id="decoration" class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-charcoal">Embroidered or Screen-Printed?</h2>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal"><strong>Embroidery</strong> uses thread, while <strong>screen printing</strong> applies an approved ink system. Compare the exact garment, artwork, placement, quantity, feel, care, setup, price, and production partner before choosing a method.</p>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">A program may use one method or more than one. Request product-specific recommendations and a current written quote. See the <a href="/services/embroidery-las-vegas/" class="text-gold-700 underline decoration-gold-500/40 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-gold-600">embroidery planning page</a> and <a href="/services/screen-printing-las-vegas/" class="text-gold-700 underline decoration-gold-500/40 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-gold-600">screen-printing planning page</a>.</p>

 <h2 id="how-many" class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-charcoal">How Many Company Shirts Per Employee?</h2>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">Set the quantity from each employee's schedule, laundering, climate, role, garment, replacement policy, and budget. Service life depends on the product, use, care, and manufacturer guidance. See <a href="/blog/how-many-shirts-per-crew-member-vegas/" class="text-gold-700 underline decoration-gold-500/40 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-gold-600">how many shirts per crew member</a>.</p>

 <h2 id="why" class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-charcoal">Why Company Shirts Matter for Trades and Service Businesses</h2>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">A branded shirt can help customers identify a trades or field-service employee. It may support a consistent presentation, but it does not guarantee trust, sales, or any business outcome.</p>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">Beyond perception, branded shirts solve practical problems: identifying which sub a worker belongs to on a multi-trade jobsite, distinguishing apprentices from journeymen, and keeping crews looking professional even when the work itself is dirty. Per the <a href="https://www.osha.gov/heat-exposure" rel="noopener" class="text-gold-700 underline decoration-gold-500/40 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-gold-600">OSHA heat exposure guidance</a>, the right fabric weight and color for desert summer work matters as much as the branding.</p>

 <h2 id="getting-started" class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-charcoal">Getting Started With Company Shirts</h2>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">If you're outfitting a crew for the first time, four decisions to make before getting a quote:</p>
 <ol class="mb-6 list-decimal pl-6 space-y-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">
 <li><strong>Garment type by role.</strong> Polos for client-facing, tees for field, work shirts for industrial laundry programs.</li>
 <li><strong>Decoration method.</strong> Embroidery or screen printing — usually a mix.</li>
 <li><strong>Quantity per employee.</strong> Set it from schedule, laundering, role, replacement policy, and budget.</li>
 <li><strong>Reorder pattern.</strong> Compare bulk orders, planned batches, and a proposed <a href="/company-stores/" class="text-gold-700 underline decoration-gold-500/40 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-gold-600">company-store configuration</a>. No platform has been selected or launched, and all capabilities require separate written approval.</li>
 </ol>

 <div class="mt-12 border border-hairline bg-panel p-7 sm:p-9">
